// terms fall like k^(s-1) and do not cancel; 64 of them leave a tail below
// 64^s/(-s) of the prefactor, 1.3e-6 at s = -3. The sine argument is
// reduced exactly: pi (2 frac(k b) + (s/2 mod 2)), minus its nearest
